/P 53 0 R
/T (Results: The themes addressed adaptive confidence, and career ownership, family priorities and everyday coping practices, and workplace recognition, mentoring, and informal support networks, and stakeholder relationships. Participants described both personal resourcefulness and organisational constraints. When self-doubt arose, participants generally described it as situational rather than enduring, and as manageable in context.)
/E (Results: The themes addressed adaptive confidence, and career ownership, family priorities and everyday coping practices, and workplace recognition, mentoring, and informal support networks, and stakeholder relationships. Participants described both personal resourcefulness and organisational constraints. When self-doubt arose, participants generally described it as situational rather than enduring, and as manageable in context.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [24]
>>
