/S /H3
/P 55 0 R
/T (The analytic dataset comprised 13 participant records from professionals working in pharmaceuticals, finance, banking, technology, consulting, human resources, entrepreneurship,  nonprofit organisations. Reported professional experience ranged from approximately 10 years to 30 years or more. Participants were experienced professionals from varied occupational contexts. Given the small qualitative sample, the findings are not statistically representative. Malterud et al. \(2016\) propose assessing information power in relation to the study aim, sample specificity, use of theory, quality of dialogue, and analytic strategy. The available notes and uneven coverage do not permit a definitive claim about sample adequacy or saturation.)
/E (The analytic dataset comprised 13 participant records from professionals working in pharmaceuticals, finance, banking, technology, consulting, human resources, entrepreneurship,  nonprofit organisations. Reported professional experience ranged from approximately 10 years to 30 years or more. Participants were experienced professionals from varied occupational contexts. Given the small qualitative sample, the findings are not statistically representative. Malterud et al. \(2016\) propose assessing information power in relation to the study aim, sample specificity, use of theory, quality of dialogue, and analytic strategy. The available notes and uneven coverage do not permit a definitive claim about sample adequacy or saturation.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
