316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Confidence in transition. Indicative codes: earned compe-    -tence; initial uncertainty; stretching beyond familiar tasks. Interpretive claim: The Confidence may be demonstrated through adaptive learning rather than the absence of apprehension. Career self-determination. Indicative codes: self-advocacy; preparation; promotion requests; sponsor visibility. Interpretive claim: Advancement accounts feature purposeful action and negotiation. Values and boundaries. Indicative codes: care responsibilities; prioritisation; time limits; career trade-offs. The Interpretive claim: Family commitments can coexist with meaningful professional ambition. Regulation & recovery. Indicative codes: exercise; hobbies; peer conversations; problem-solving. Interpretive claim: Everyday practices may support perspective but cannot substitute for healthy work design. Organisational voice. Indicative codes: respectful management; perceived bias; inclusion in decisions; recognition. Interpretive claim: Workplace environments may also influence whether the capabilities are heard and rewarded. Relational leadership. Indicative codes: mentorship; and coaching; networks; stakeholder influence; developing others. Interpretive claim: Supportive relationships may connect self-management with collective leadership.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
